@* ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
   One icon component, one icon font.

   The app was running three icon systems at once: emoji literals in the
   markup, Radzen's icon font via `Icon="..."` on its own components, and the
   Material Symbols font — which index.html loads on every page but which
   exactly one element used. Emoji were the worst of the three: they ignore
   `color`, so a status glyph could not be tinted to match the state it
   reported; they render as a different drawing per operating system; and they
   cannot be sized off the type scale.

   Material Symbols wins because it is already downloaded (Radzen's own icons
   ARE Material Symbols, so `Icon="refresh"` on a RadzenButton and
   <PtIcon Name="refresh" /> draw the same glyph from the same file).

   Sizing is relative — `1.25em` of whatever the icon sits next to — so an icon
   in a heading and an icon in a caption are each correct without being told.
   ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── *@

<span class="pt-icon @SizeClass @(Filled ? "pt-icon-filled" : null) @Class"
      aria-hidden="@(Label is null ? "true" : null)"
      role="@(Label is null ? null : "img")"
      aria-label="@Label"
      translate="no">@Name</span>

@code {
    /// <summary>Material Symbols ligature name, e.g. "refresh", "wifi_off", "science".</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Name { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>
    /// Accessible name. Leave null — the default — for decorative icons that sit beside
    /// a text label; the icon is then hidden from assistive tech rather than read out as
    /// a duplicate of the word next to it.
    /// </summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Label { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Optical size. "sm" | "md" (default) | "lg" | "xl".</summary>
    [Parameter] public string Size { get; set; } = "md";

    /// <summary>Solid rather than outlined — reserve for selected/active states.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Filled { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }

    private string? SizeClass => Size switch
    {
        "sm" => "pt-icon-sm",
        "lg" => "pt-icon-lg",
        "xl" => "pt-icon-xl",
        _ => null
    };
}
